Feature: Masking Invoice Numbers in d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background:
    Given the table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue exists
    And the table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone does not exist

  Scenario: Clone d_product_revenue table to d_product_revenue_clone
    When the d_product_revenue_clone table is to be created
    Then the table is created as a replica of d_product_revenue

  Scenario: Mask last 4 digits of Invoice Numbers in invoice_number column
    Given the table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone is created
    When PySpark logic is executed to mask invoice numbers
    Then the last four digits of each invoice_number are replaced with '****'

  Scenario Outline: Validate successful masking of invoice numbers
    Given the invoice_number is '<original_invoice_number>'
    When the PySpark logic is applied on the column
    Then the result should be '<masked_invoice_number>'
  
    Examples:
      | original_invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534              | 123423****            |
      | 9876543210              | 987654****            |
      | 1111222233              | 111122****            |

  Scenario Outline: Handle error on invalid data type
    Given the invoice_number is '<invalid_invoice_number>'
    When PySpark logic is applied
    Then an error message "Invalid data type for invoice_number" should be shown
  
    Examples:
      | invalid_invoice_number |
      | null                   |
      | abc123xyz              |
      | 1234.5678              |

  Scenario: Verify access rights for table operations
    Given the user executing PySpark logic
    When permissions are checked for dropping and creating tables
    Then user must have rights to perform table operations in Unity Catalog: purgo_playground

  Scenario: Ensure backup and recovery protocols
    Given a table is dropped
    When an error occurs during the drop
    Then a backup exists to restore the table

  Scenario: Check data type of invoice_number column
    Given the schema of table purgo_playground.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue
    When checking the data type of invoice_number
    Then it should be confirmed as bigint
